CommitProof mutant M5 — standby-slots-cleared (CONTRACT §9.2, ADR-0007)

Intent: setSynchronizedStandbySlots
(go/services/multipooler/internal/manager/pg_replication.go:600) always
writes synchronized_standby_slots = '' instead of the committed cohort's
physical slots.
Failure mode modelled: logical decoding runs ahead of the cohort — with
slot-based replication the primary lists the cohort's physical slots in
synchronized_standby_slots so that a logical consumer never receives a
change the standbys do not have (S13); without it, a consumer can receive
a transaction that a failover to a standby then discards (a phantom
change; S12's goal "no loss of data during a failover" presupposes the
gating).
Sources: S13, S12.
Detection (§9.2, ADR-0030): directed schedule D5 (W7 consumer, W4 load;
F1b with A = the followers' nodes for 20 s, then F2a and F2b on the leader;
F1b healed first, the old leader's pooler 30 s later, then its
PostgreSQL); expected C7 cdc-phantom.
Function touched: setSynchronizedStandbySlots (one function).

diff --git a/go/services/multipooler/internal/manager/pg_replication.go b/go/services/multipooler/internal/manager/pg_replication.go
index 1bd0238..dc53579 100644
